# Rust
target/
Cargo.lock

# Override common global gitignore patterns that match dodder/madder
# state directories. Many users have `~/.config/git/ignore` lines like
# `.dodder/` (dodder's own state dirs are typically uninteresting noise
# in personal repos). That global pattern silently masks fixture
# contamination: any process that writes to a fixture's `.dodder/` or
# `.madder/` succeeds without git noticing, and the test suite then
# reads the contaminated state on subsequent runs. Re-include the
# fixture trees explicitly so `git status` flags any drift.
!zz-tests_bats/previous_versions/*/.dodder/
!zz-tests_bats/previous_versions/*/.dodder/**
!zz-tests_bats/previous_versions/*/.madder/
!zz-tests_bats/previous_versions/*/.madder/**
